  "number": 29,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "Decouple v0.scale from E8M0 and refactor SAIL into dispatch functions",
  "user": {
    "login": "ptomsich",
    "id": 14983582,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTgzNTgy",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14983582?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/ptomsich",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ptomsich/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## Summary                                                                                                                                                                                                    \r\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                \r\n  - **Decouple `v0.scale` from the E8M0 scale format.** The `v0.scale`                                                                                                                                          \r\n    mechanism now specifies only that paired block-scale factors are\r\n    present in `v0`; the scale format is an inherent property of the                                                                                                                                            \r\n    input data type (e.g., MXFP8 = OFP8 + E8M0 scales), not of the                                                                                                                                              \r\n    encoding. A new \"Scale formats\" subsection defines E8M0 explicitly\r\n    and leaves room for future formats. All generic microscaling prose,                                                                                                                                         \r\n    the `v0` layout description, and per-instruction descriptions are\r\n    now format-agnostic.                                                                                                                                                                                        \r\n                  \r\n  - **Refactor SAIL into four top-level dispatch functions.** The main\r\n    loop bodies from all 11 GEMM instruction SAIL blocks are extracted\r\n    into `int_gemm`, `fp_gemm`, `fp_scaled_gemm`, and                                                                                                                                                           \r\n    `int_scaled_gemm`. Each instruction's Operation block is now a thin\r\n    wrapper: legality checks → `decode_gemm_geometry` → format setup →                                                                                                                                          \r\n    single dispatch call. For FP widening instructions, the dispatch is                                                                                                                                         \r\n    conditional on `vm`, directly mirroring the hardware decode.\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                \r\n  - **Generalize scale width for future formats.** Introduce\r\n    `scale_width_of(scale_fmt)` to derive the per-scale bit width and\r\n    pair width from the scale format, replacing hardcoded 16-bit                                                                                                                                                \r\n    assumptions in the stride computation (`R = λ × SEW / pw`), the\r\n    `v0` capacity proof, and the legality constraint                                                                                                                                                            \r\n    (`SEW × λ ≥ pw`). The SAIL helper `read_block_scales` reads                                                                                                                                                 \r\n    `pw`-bit elements and extracts `sw`-bit halves generically. All\r\n    call sites pass `E8M0` explicitly; existing behavior is unchanged.                      ",
